About The Role
As the Regional Director, Policy & Partnerships, you will provide support and oversight to the entire programs within Group Nigeria. You are responsible for building and managing diverse stakeholder relationships, and focused on account management and sustaining our work and operations.
You’ll be taking over existing relationships from the Policy and Partnerships Programme Development teams and other Executives, and make these your own to ensure close collaboration and on-time execution of the programs.
This entails significant relationship management, as well as project management in ensuring data and approvals needed to pass between the government and programs do so in a timely way for program deadlines.
You will ensure that the government partners understand the programs, and support its implementation. This will require coordination of stakeholder sessions, government workshops, and government public events and celebrations.
During government workshops, there will be a need for careful engagement and collaboration on programme details -- to be successful in this role, you must learn about all aspects of our programming, and what can be negotiated and what cannot to ensure we deliver on what the government requires of us -- improved learning outcomes.
You will need to be diplomatic and have discretion; know when to speak and when to listen
What You Will Do
Provide support for the Group MD regarding advocacy with the Government (Executive, Legislative and Judiciary at the federal, state and local government levels) on various market-friendly policies
Map all key government officials, and create robust stakeholder management plans for each
Regularly monitor regulations and policies relevant to NewGlobe and our partners nationally and at sub-national levels
Scanning the education policy environment with a bid to guiding and influencing policy
Work closely with the Group MD to build and manage the Group Nigeria Board of Advisors as a unique sponsor/influencer body for our in-country government programmes
Secure strategic relationships within the newly inaugurated Federal administration that are relevant to the achieving the objectives of NewGlobe at a national level.Help build partnerships, relationships and execute strategies to sustain our goals across programs.
Work closely with the Programme Development counterparts and regional leadership, be responsible for overseeing key government relationships and programming. To do this, you’ll lead government engagement, training and stakeholder meetings.
Ensure creation of governance committees according to core programming guidelines, and establish a regular meeting schedule.
Ensure thorough weekly and monthly reporting to the government begins and is continued under permanent programme leadership.
Manage and oversee all Policy and Partnerships program staff (focussed on Programme Management).
Manage the diverse strategic stakeholders across multiple Government departments and levels within those departments; with prominent education ecosystem stakeholders, including but not limited to the local and national teacher labour unions; and important 'influencers’ to ensure the successful and popular launch of the government’s new programmes.
Establish and implement short- and long-range goals, objectives, policies and operating procedures for the government relations support function; monitor and evaluates program effectiveness; effects changes required for improvement;
Work with key stakeholders on consultative efforts to drive reforms in delivery of education to underserved communities;
Utilize lead management techniques and maintain a detailed and dynamic database of these key influencer communities while tracking progress of programme launch;
What You Should Have
Bachelor's degree with superior academic performance;
Over 8 years’ experience in government program delivery or working in account management or as an engagement manager;
In depth experience building and systematically managing key complex relationships and accounts to ensure program delivery in a complex, multi-stakeholder program or project;
Previous experience working with a Ministry of Education on program delivery, preferred; If not within education, experience with another government delivery program or project, such as in health or ICT;
Confidence, authority, and level-headed decision making needed as the leadership voice for the program;
Knowledge of local, state and federal government issues related to the provision of primary education in the country would be preferred;
Ability to balance commercial interests and social benefits - a blend across business and political acumen, but also high emotional intelligence and relationship-building skills;
Experience acting as an on-the-record spokesperson;
Highly capable and thoughtful problem-solving skills; able to act as an intermediary and a solutions driven lead, to ensure effective collaboration and communication between the Government client and our organization;
Prior experience within a fast-paced, high-growth, metric-driven operational organization will be an advantage;
You’re also
A detailed doer – You have a track record of getting things done. You’re organized and responsive. You take ownership of every idea you touch and execute it to a fine level of detail, setting targets, engaging others, and doing whatever it takes to get the job done. You can multi-task dozens of such projects at once and never lose sight of the details. Likely, you have some experience in a start-up or other rapid-growth company.
A networking mastermind – You excel at meeting new people and turning them into advocates. You communicate in a clear, conscientious, and effective way in both written and oral speech. You can influence strangers in the course of a single conversation. Allies and colleagues will go to bat for your ideas. You have an existing network from prior experience in the country, preferably in the regulatory, education, or business sectors.
A creative problem-solver – Growing any business from scratch comes with massive and constant challenges. On top of that, NewGlobe works in often fragile, sometimes volatile low-resource communities and with complex government systems. You need to be flexible and ready to get everything done effectively, quickly, and affordably with the materials at hand.
A relentless advocate –The children we serve and teachers we empower never leave your mind. You know them, get them, have shared a meal with them (or would be happy to in the future). You would never shrink back from shaking a parent’s hand or picking up a crying child, no matter what the person was wearing or looked like. Every decision you make considers their benefit, experience, and value.
A malleable learner –You believe you can always do better. You welcome constructive criticism and provide it freely to others. You know you only get better tomorrow when others point out where you’ve missed things or failed today.
A data-driven decision-maker – When making decisions, you don’t rely on your intuition alone. You collect data, you analyze it and make decisions with clear justifications.
A curious investigator – You ask why a lot. You don’t just take what you see and accept it. You wonder why it is that way, and are aware that the world we see is created by human choices and actions – and it could be different. You wonder, and see the world as wonderful even when you want to change a part of it that is unjust.

Action Against Hunger is currently looking to fill the role of an Advocacy and Communication Officer who will be responsible to play a crucial role in developing and implementing effective advocacy and communication strategies to raise awareness about our programming, to create and disseminate engaging content, materials, and tools that showcase our impact and mission. Work closely with our field team to integrate new approaches, tools, and techniques into our programming, ensuring our message reaches a wider audience.
Reporting to:
Head of Department Advocacy and Communication
Proposed start date:
September 2024
Work location:
Abuja, FCT
Key Responsibilities
The Advocacy and Communication Officer is responsible:
Liaise closely with the field advocacy team to develop and support the integration of new communication approaches, tools, and techniques into Action Against Hunger programming;
Organize and coordinate the celebration of international/national advocacy days and campaigns, and use such forums for allowed advocacy themes (e.g. World Humanitarian Day, World Breastfeeding Day, International Women Day, Global Handwashing Day, etc);
Support Action Against Hunger advocacy efforts by developing advocacy messages, materials, tools as well as multimedia content – photography and videography skills needed;
Undertake field visits to monitor the impact of the communication materials, messaging, use of tools, identifying communication gaps and opportunities for a wider spread and reach critical masses with appropriate information;
Assist the advocacy and communications team with the coordination of field advocacy events, meetings, and where possible representations;
Update mainstream and social media platforms to communicate program activities to a wider audience;
Support coordination with and work with mapped out media and communication organizations in implementing programs’ advocacy activities;
Monitoring and supervision of media as part of advocacy-related collaborative activities and plans in Nigeria by ensuring that these are in line with Action Against Hunger country strategy;
Liaise with the project team for advocacy and communications needs and raise procurement requests for the production of IEC materials and other visibility materials;
Contribute to the state and national level advocacy agenda by collecting and providing evidence that advantages project outcomes;
Collect and document beneficiary stories and testimonies that can be used for advocacy at a national and international level;
Promote cross-thematic learning through facilitating engagements, and knowledge sharing workshops on advocacy and communications;
Perform additional activities as requested by the Head of Department Advocacy and Communications;
Lead in content gathering for mission newsletter;
Proactively cultivate relationships with key media contacts and compile and maintain contacts and a general database of stakeholders;
Manage Action Against Hunger image and video library for communication, reporting, and other needs;
Liaise with media outlets to package information and ensure external visibility with appropriate information and message targeting, while working with HoD Advocacy and Communications and a wider audience, contribute to the preparation of talking points, media briefs, and press releases;
Support in maintaining a good relationship with Government and non-Government partners working on the Project through effective representations and delegated responsibilities.
Organize learning, knowledge sharing, and training for program and field teams on innovating and new digital and advocacy technologies;
Support the timely dissemination of program information internally and externally;
Work with the Knowledge Management Officer and field program team to ensure success/impact stories are valid and qualitative;
Work with field program teams in Action Against Hunger field bases to plan and execute proper closeout activities;
Manage stakeholders’ relationships relevant to advocacy and communications by projecting Action Against Hunger brand values and virtues.
Position Requirement:
Education Qualification:
Minimum of Bachelor’s degree in Media Studies, Communications, Development Communication, or relevant discipline in fields of ACF thematic implementations (Health, FSL, WASH, etc);
At least 2 years of relevant experience in communications and advocacy;
A demonstrable understanding and experience of NGO media/advocacy work in the humanitarian or development context;
Experience in designing and leading media campaigns or communication strategies;
Experience in capacity building and/or training skills is highly advantageous;
Ability to produce a variety of written and visual communications products in a clear, concise style;
Highly skilled in photography, videography, infographic design, and editing, with proficiency in using Adobe Premiere, Photoshop, Canva, CapCut, etc. Candidates will be tested on these skills;
Ability to deliver oral presentations to various audiences;
Ability to work in partnership with government and development partners;
Ability to maintain good relationships with media outlets;
Ability to develop, design, or create new ideas, relationships, systems, or products;
High level interpersonal and diplomatic skills along with awareness of political and cultural sensitivities in different settings of Nigeria;
Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues to achieve team and organizational goals;
Strong skills in graphic design skills and the ability to develop simple infographics are desirable;
Strong skills in Microsoft Office (Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint, Word);
Fluency in written and spoken English;
Fluency in the Hausa language is an advantage;
Willingness and ability to travel regularly within remote areas, where services are limited.
