Job Summary
By virtue of the Delta State Polytechnic, Ogwashi-Uku Law 2002, the Librarian is a Principal Officer responsible to the Rector for the Library Services of the Polytechnic.
The Person
The Polytechnic Librarian is the Chief Library Officer and shall be responsible to the Rector for the administration of the Polytechnic Library and the coordination of the Library Services in the teaching units of the Polytechnic. He/she is one of the Principal Officers of the Polytechnic.
In addition to proven experience in Library management and leadership, the successful candidate must have a demonstrable passion for academic endeavors and must also be credible.
Requirements
The candidate for the post must possess the following qualifications and qualities:
Master's Degree from a recognized Institution in Library Science or Library and Information Science, while possession of Doctorate Degree [Ph.D.] will be an added advantage;
Have a minimum of Second Class Lower Division Degree or a minimum of Lower Credit in Higher National Diploma (HND) in Library Science or Library and Information Science from a recognized Institution;
Minimum of eighteen (18) years cognate experience in tertiary Institutions, at least ten (10) years of which must have been gained in a Polytechnic or similar TVET Institutions;
Currently on the rank of a Chief Librarian, from the Polytechnic sector with not less than five (5) years experience on the rank;
Demonstrate evidence of strong academic and administrative leadership, initiative, and creativity in Library policy formulation, good human relations, and positive managerial attributes;
Provide evidence of membership of professional body/bodies in Library recognized by the Federal Government;
Provide evidence of scholarly publications in reputable journals as well as presentation of invited papers at educational/library conferences, seminars, and workshops;
Person who is not likely to pursue, racial, gender, political, religious, or other sectional interests;
Morally sound, of impeccable character, proven integrity, and free from financial embarrassment;
Physically and mentally fit (with evidence from a Government hospital);
Proficient in Information & Communication Technology (ICT);
Not more than fifty-nine (59) years of age as of the date of publication of the advert.
Terms of Appointment and Conditions of Service
The appointment is for a single tenure of five (5) years in line with extant provisions. The salary is consolidated and the appointee shall enjoy any other benefits attached to the position of a Principal Officer of the Polytechnic as approved by the State Government.

Our client, a leading full-service commercial law Firm, is seeking a highly motivated and experienced Senior Associate to lead its Energy & Project Finance Team.
The role holder will work closely with financial institutions, stakeholders and clients to structure and negotiate project finance transactions, and ensure compliance with legal requirements.
Responsibilities:
Leading the energy and project finance team on diverse transactions;
Advising on the structuring of project finance transactions, such as infrastructure, public-private partnership, debt debenture, bonds, private equity, and other related financing arrangements;
Working closely with financial institutions, project developers, and other stakeholders to facilitate smooth transaction processes;
Conducting legal due diligence on behalf of client;
Drafting, reviewing, and negotiating key documents such as loan agreements, security documents, and project agreements;
Ensuring compliance with relevant laws, regulations, and industry standards;
Regularly providing clients with industry updates and legal opinions on industry trends; identifying potential legal risks and mitigation strategies;
Keeping abreast of trends in the industry;
Contributing to the business development of the Practice Area; amongst others.
Specifications:
Bachelor's degree in LLB, BL
LLM will be an added advantage
Minimum of 8 years post-call experience, preferably in the Energy and/or Finance sector
Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills
Exceptional writing and verbal communication skills
Excellent negotiation skills
Strong understanding of project finance structures and documentation
Excellent team building and management skills
Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)

Job Responsibilities:
Complete the design, coding, testing and writing of relevant documents according to the development specifications and processes;
Solve technical problems during the development process;
Participate in code maintenance;
Maintain and upgrade existing software products, quickly locate and repair existing software defects;
Able to quickly understand and use new technologies to accomplish set goals.
Job requirements:
1. Familiar with JAVA language, with more than 2 years of experience in writing web applications or project development using Java is preferred;
2. Familiar with the use and configuration of open source frameworks and components such as Spring, Spring boot, JPA, Hibernate, Quartz, Redis, ActiveMq, etc.
3. Have a deep understanding of multi-threading and network requests, and be familiar with distributed related concepts and principles.
4. Familiar with the encoding and processing of JSON, XML, CSV and other data formats;
5. Solid database foundation, familiar with SQL syntax, familiar with MySQL, and have a certain understanding of Oracle;
6. Familiar with Linux operating system, Maven, Git code management, and experience in multi-branch parallel development is preferred;
7. Good programming style and technical specifications, high learning, acceptance and communication skills, strong expression ability, teamwork spirit, self-motivated candidates are preferred.

